{%- comment -%}
  Renders the plus icon.

  Source: phase-3-assets/icons/icon-plus.svg, drawn in Phase 3 — 24x24 canvas,
  stroke 1.5, currentColor, round caps and joins.

  Round, not square. Phase 2 §18.3 rule 2 specifies square caps and mitred
  joins; every glyph Phase 3 drew and Phases 4-7 shipped uses round ones, so
  matching the set is what keeps the icons looking like one drawing. The
  deviation belongs to the set, not to this file, and is recorded in
  PHASE-8-PRODUCT-SHOPPING-UX.md rather than half-corrected here.

  Accepts:
  - class: {String} optional extra class names

  Usage:
  {% render 'icon-plus' %}

  Decorative: the wrapping button carries the accessible name. Phase 2 §18.1
  names plus and minus as required rather than optional, because without them
  the quantity selector of §12.4 cannot be built. Phase 3 drew them; Phase 8 is
  the first phase with an interaction that needs them, so this is where they
  enter the theme.
{%- endcomment -%}
<svg class="icon icon--plus {{ class }}" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 4.75v14.5"/><path d="M4.75 12h14.5"/></svg>
